+# Privacy inventory and deployment
+
+Reviewed November 4, 2026. Scope: the two static HTML pages, CSS, image,
+package scripts, and HTTP header configuration. No browser or live network
+audit was performed.
+
+| Component | Data and recipients | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| HTML and CSS | Requests to the site's hosting operator | Necessary to deliver public content; no personal fields |
+| Hero photo | Previously sent visitor IP, request metadata, and potentially referrer to images.unsplash.com | Downloaded existing stock photo into assets/coffee-hero.jpg; no runtime third-party request |
+| JavaScript, analytics, advertising, embeds, fonts | None | No client scripts or runtime dependencies; CSP blocks execution and connections |
+| Cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB, service workers | None | No identifiers, tokens, account data, or preferences stored by this site |
+| Account/order/logout links | Navigation placeholders; no backend in this repository | Do not present as implemented authentication or checkout |
+| Hosting logs | Host may receive IP address, URL, user agent, and other request metadata | Operator must set and document minimal logging and retention before production |
+
+Photo source (build-time download only):
+https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085
+The site's system font stack makes no font-provider requests.
+
+## Build and HTTP enforcement
+
+Run `npm run build` with Node 20+. It audits the public sources and creates a
+public-only `dist/` directory, including `_headers`. No server is started.
+`netlify.toml` configures Netlify to publish this directory and honor the headers.
+Hosts supporting the same `_headers` format can also publish `dist/`.
+On other hosts, explicitly map `security-headers.json` to actual HTTP response
+headers. A plain static file server (including the existing local `start`
+command) may ignore `_headers`.
+
+CSP and referrer meta tags provide partial fallback when headers are unavailable.
+Framing protection, Permissions-Policy, HSTS, nosniff, and cross-origin response
+policies require real HTTP headers. See the [CSP specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directive-frame-ancestors)
+for the restriction on `frame-ancestors` in meta policies.
+Serve production over HTTPS and redirect HTTP at the hosting layer. HSTS starts
+at 300 seconds; increase after confirming HTTPS works. Subdomain and preload
+commitments require a separate domain audit.
+
+The CSP denies scripts, fetch/beacons/WebSockets, workers, frames, forms, plugins,
+and fonts, and allows only same-origin CSS and images. Styles were moved out of
+inline markup so no `unsafe-inline` exception is needed. No reporting endpoint
+is configured: browser reports can contain URLs and other personal information,
+and this repository has no secure receiver or report retention policy.
+
+## Review on every resource or data-flow change
+
+The build audit rejects scripts, forms, external URLs, embeds, imports, and
+unreviewed asset types. It is a conservative static regression guard, not a
+complete HTML/CSS parser or proof of hosting behavior. Review all HTML/CSS
+resource channels and HTTP policies when changing its rules. Review hosting
+injections and runtime dependencies at deployment and at least quarterly.
+Keep a record of each vendor's purpose, transferred fields, subprocessors,
+retention, deletion support, consent needs, and review date before adding it.
+Prefer local assets and static links. Optional services must stay unloaded
+until affirmative consent; revocation must stop future collection.
+
+## Requirements before implementing personal-data services
+
+- Request only fields needed for the current purpose, explain them beside the
+  input, allow guest checkout, and define retention/deletion before collecting.
+- Validate and authorize on the server; rate-limit sensitive endpoints. Use
+  HTTPS, POST bodies for sensitive fields, and never put secrets in URLs or logs.
+- Keep session identifiers server-managed with `__Host-` cookies, `Secure`,
+  `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`, `Path=/`, and no Domain attribute. Protect state
+  changes with CSRF defenses. Never put tokens or personal data in browser storage.
+- Implement logout on the server: invalidate the session, expire its cookie,
+  send `Cache-Control: no-store` and `Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"`
+  over HTTPS. Do not emulate logout with browser storage cleanup alone.
+- Set `Cache-Control: no-store` on authenticated/personal responses. Minimize and
+  redact hosting/application logs, including query strings and authorization
+  fields; define restricted access and a short documented retention period.
+- Provide working access, correction, export, and deletion flows alongside
+  registration. Update the public privacy notice with real operator contact and
+  retention details before launching collection. The existing contact route is
+  a placeholder, not an implemented data-rights channel.
+
+These are future backend requirements; this static build does not implement
+accounts, cookies, API protections, or control the hosting provider's logs.
